		"text": "The Bura and the Pabir (Babur) of southern Borno speak one Chadic language in two dialects, though they see themselves as distinct peoples; most Pabir are Muslim and most Bura Christian. They are the main people of Biu and Shani, and also speak Hausa, Kibaku and Marghi.",
